  "implementation": {
    "src/orze/core/cpu_execution.py": "Only optional exact-int 1..32 proposal_page_size in explicitly version-2 custom policy declarations; omitted v1/old-v2 declarations retain their existing shapes. Existing policy fingerprint binds the opt-in.",
    "src/orze/core/research_interfaces.py": "BoundPolicy recognizes exact ReadProposals{kind,cursor} and SelectProposals{kind,request_ids} only with explicit opt-in, checks against its private pre-callback capture, accepts bounded unique request IDs rather than callback-supplied results.",
    "src/orze/core/cpu_proposal_requests.py": "New read-only records_page uses one schema check, scope-bound BINARY request_id keyset LIMIT n+1, fully decodes every returned row including lookahead, and performs one bounded IN query for selection. Returns requested order and explicit missing IDs; internal database identity is not exposed to Policy. Legacy records_view/schema unchanged.",
    "src/orze/engine/cpu_proposals.py": "ProposalPager shares the invocation's exact existing EvidencePager revision guard but owns independent cursor/position and bounded page state. Historical outcomes are not revalidated as current authority. Legacy recorded_proposals remains unchanged.",
    "src/orze/engine/cpu_phase.py": "Opt-in pager integration in the same loop; all four read decisions continue without ingress, budget reservation, claim, worker, or --once dispatch consumption. Proposal continuations re-read the currently displayed evidence result/unavailable fullRefs through EvidencePager selection; empty evidence pages verify the guard. Normal decisions release both bounded scan states."
  },
